.TH SHADDAI-FONTS 1 "November 2026" "exec" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shaddai-fonts, shaddai \- preview and save Linux virtual-console fonts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY shaddai
.RI [ font-directory ]
.YS
.SY shaddai
.B \-\-tutorial
.YS
.SY shaddai
.B \-\-default
.YS
.SY shaddai
.B \-\-help
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shaddai
uses
.BR setfont (8)
from kbd to preview bitmap fonts on a numbered Linux virtual console
such as
.IR /dev/tty2 .
.B shaddai-fonts
is another name for the same command.
An optional directory supplies the fonts.
When available among the fonts being browsed,
.B Lat2-Terminus16.psfu.gz
is the first preview.
.PP
Quitting with
.BR q ,
end of input, or a handled signal restores the original font and Unicode
map unless a preview has already been kept.
Press Enter to keep the preview and choose whether to save it for this TTY,
all TTYs, or the current session only.
A font belongs to the console, so the setting affects everyone using that TTY.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-tutorial
Show a five-page tour of the files and commands that control console
fonts. On a terminal it is interactive. With piped input or output,
it prints all five pages.
.TP
.B \-\-default
Save
.B Lat2-Terminus16.psfu.gz
as the shared font and apply the saved choices to allocated virtual consoles.
This mode works with nonterminal standard input and skips the chooser.
It can be called from setup scripts.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR n ", " p
Preview the next or previous font.
.TP
.B /
Filter by filename. An empty filter restores the full list.
.TP
.B d
Toggle double size. Doubling requires a font at most 16 by 16 pixels.
.TP
.BR h ", " ?
Open the tutorial.
.TP
.B Enter
Keep the preview and choose whether to save it.
.TP
.B q
Restore the original font and quit.
.SH PERSISTENCE
Temporary previews require kbd. Saving requires systemd and root access.
The command requests sudo authentication when needed.
.PP
A TTY-specific font takes priority over the shared default. Saving a new
shared default preserves TTY-specific choices. Each saved PSF contains the
loaded glyphs and Unicode map, including any doubling, and can be loaded
independently of the original font files.
.PP
Saving installs a loader and two systemd drop-ins. The drop-ins append
loader calls after
.B systemd-vconsole-setup.service
and before
.B getty@.service
login prompts, including the
.B autovt@
alias. Font failures are logged and login proceeds.
The boot hook uses
.I /dev/vcsN
to find allocated consoles. The getty hook covers later allocations.
Both use the installed loader directly.
.PP
Native systemd configuration lives in
.IR /etc/vconsole.conf .
On NixOS, the
.B console.font
option generates the native font setting.
Shaddai loads its choices after native setup, leaving the keymap and
generated files intact. This applies after the initramfs stage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/consolefonts/shaddai/ttyN.psf
Saved font for
.IR /dev/ttyN .
.TP
.I /etc/consolefonts/shaddai/default.psf
Shared fallback for consoles without a TTY-specific font.
.TP
.I /etc/consolefonts/shaddai/*.psf.previous
Previous saved choice, kept when a saved PSF is replaced.
.TP
.I /usr/local/libexec/shaddai-console-font
Installed copy of
.I lib/shaddai/console-font
from the checkout.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/systemd-vconsole-setup.service.d/90-shaddai-font.conf
Apply saved choices to allocated consoles after native setup.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/getty@.service.d/90-shaddai-font.conf
Apply the choice for a console before its getty starts.
.SH EXAMPLES
Inspect the units and the installed loader.
.EX
systemctl cat systemd-vconsole-setup.service getty@tty2.service
cat /usr/local/libexec/shaddai-console-font
.EE
.PP
Apply the saved font to a VT allocated without getty.
.EX
sudo /usr/local/libexec/shaddai-console-font /dev/tty2
.EE
.SH RECOVERY
Remove a TTY-specific PSF to inherit the shared font, or remove the shared
PSF to use the native default on consoles without a TTY-specific choice.
Restart native console setup to apply the change.
.EX
sudo rm /etc/consolefonts/shaddai/tty2.psf
sudo rm /etc/consolefonts/shaddai/default.psf
sudo systemctl restart systemd-vconsole-setup.service
.EE
.PP
To recover a replaced choice, copy the
.I .psf.previous
file over its
.I .psf
file and run the loader. To remove the integration completely, remove both
drop-ins and the installed loader listed above, then run
.BR "sudo systemctl daemon-reload" .
All recovery operations work without launching the chooser.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setfont (8),
.BR systemd-vconsole-setup.service (8),
.BR vconsole.conf (5)
